# `optim::adam_state_like`

Creates a zeroed `AdamState` for a list of parameters.

## Signature

```cpp
optim::AdamState optim::adam_state_like(const std::vector<pluss::Series> &params);
```

## What It Does

Returns a state whose `m`, `v` and `max_v` are zero with the shape, dtype and platform of each parameter, and `step` is zero. `adam_step` creates one automatically if the state it is given does not match the parameters, so call this only to hold the state yourself.

## Parameters

`params`
: The parameters to match.

## Returns

A zeroed `AdamState`.

## Practical Examples

### Example 1

One block.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace optim = pluss::subsp::math::optim;
using Pack = optim::ParameterPack<pluss::Series>;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const optim::AdamState state = optim::adam_state_like({pluss::series::make({1.0, 2.0, 3.0})});
  out.writeln("m =", state.m[0].items<double>(), ", step =", state.step);
}
```

### Example 2

Two blocks of different shapes.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace optim = pluss::subsp::math::optim;
using Pack = optim::ParameterPack<pluss::Series>;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  const optim::AdamState state = optim::adam_state_like({pluss::series::make({1.0, 2.0}), pluss::make_series(5.0)});
  out.writeln("blocks =", state.v.size(), ", first size =", state.v[0].numel(), ", second size =", state.v[1].numel());
}
```

### Example 3

A complex parameter keeps its dtype.

@@run@@
```cpp
#include <pluss/ma.h>
#include <pluss/tils/kit/output.h>

#include <complex>

using namespace pluss::tils;

namespace optim = pluss::subsp::math::optim;
using Pack = optim::ParameterPack<pluss::Series>;
using pluss::Series;

int main() {
  OutputEngine out;
  out.print_defaults(PrintOptions{}.fixed(4));
  using C = std::complex<double>;
  const optim::AdamState state = optim::adam_state_like({pluss::make_series(std::vector<C>{{1.0, 2.0}}, {1})});
  out.writeln("complex moment =", state.m[0].items<C>()[0].real(), "+", state.m[0].items<C>()[0].imag(), "i");
}
```

